# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source GIS data and derived geometry are NOT committed.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. Committing verbatim Town of Blacksburg GIS data, or
# geometry derived from it, is redistribution — and no town dataset grants any reuse
# right (copyrightText is empty on every layer). See docs/05-licensing-status.md,
# release gate G1.
#
# Separately, households.json and unassociated-households.json contain ~18,000
# individual residential street addresses. Those must not be published regardless of
# how the licensing question is answered.
#
# What IS committed: the pipeline code, the snapshot sidecars (metadata about the
# data — field names, counts, URLs, edit dates), the build report, and the aggregate
# review files. Anyone with network access can reproduce the rest in a few minutes:
#
#   python3 -m pipeline.sources.fetch
#   python3 -m pipeline.build.run
#   python3 -m pipeline.build.campus_report
#   python3 -m pipeline.build.map_export
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw source snapshots — verbatim town GIS data.
pipeline/snapshots/**/*.geojson

# Derived geometry. Every generated map embeds it, and complex-review-map.html also
# embeds one point per residential unit — household coordinates.
pipeline/out/**/*.geojson
pipeline/out/**/*.html

# Address-level records — privacy, not just licensing.
pipeline/out/**/households.json
pipeline/out/**/review/unassociated-households.json

# Routing prototype outputs. benchmark.json and quality-review.json are aggregate
# metrics and are committed; the route visualisation embeds derived network geometry
# and is not.
api/routing/results/*.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 3 — application
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Participant data. The database holds names, emails and token hashes, and it is a
# runtime artifact, not source. It must never be committed regardless of tier.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Secrets. BPW_TOKEN_PEPPER and BPW_DATABASE_URL are supplied by the environment or
# a managed secret store; a committed .env would put a working credential in git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output and dependencies.
node_modules/
web/dist/
web/dev-dist/
.pytest_cache/
.vitest/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Codespace-generated secrets. Created by .devcontainer/setup.sh, never committed.
.codespace-env
